    "detailed_reasoning": "1. In-domain verification CONFIRMED: 100.00% accuracy and 1.0000 macro-F1 on fruit_identifier_v1/test.json (N=2,882). 2. Zero physical split leakage: test images share 0 paths and 0 exact SHA-256 hashes with training/validation sets. 3. Dataset-source shortcut learning EMPIRICALLY CONFIRMED: Each target class was trained exclusively on a single dataset (Guava from Sindh SAU, Banana from BananaID, Apple from Apple Mendeley, Mango from Harumanis). When evaluated on unseen out-of-domain sources of the exact same botanical species (FruitNet Guava, FruitNet Banana, FruitNet Apple), the model severely degrades, frequently classifying them as 'negative_background' because the model associated FruitNet camera/compression/tabletop signatures with the negative class. 4. Architectural Solution Required: Multi-dataset cross-source training, background augmentation (CutMix/Mosaic), and a Stage 1A YOLOv8n object detection localization step to crop isolated fruit boundaries and eliminate background context shortcuts before species classification."
